<div class="ui ui-settings">
  <p class="ui__title">Machines</p>
  <div class="ui__machine">
    <span>
      <strong>laptop</strong>
      <span class="ui__quiet">you, dials in on port 24817</span>
    </span>
    <span class="ui__line">
      <span class="ui__button">Connect</span>
      <span class="ui__button">Edit</span>
      <span class="ui__button">Remove</span>
    </span>
  </div>
  <div class="ui__card">
    <p class="ui__card-top">
      <span>
        <strong>Connect laptop</strong>
        <span class="ui__dot ui__dot-bad"></span>
        Waiting: it has not connected to this server, or its link
        dropped. Nothing answers on port 24817.
      </span>
      <span class="ui__button">Close</span>
    </p>
    <p class="ui__card-top">
      <span>
        1. On laptop, run this in a terminal and leave it running.
        That machine must be able to log in to the server over SSH.
      </span>
      <span class="ui__button">Copy</span>
    </p>
    <p class="ui__code">
      ssh -N -o ExitOnForwardFailure=yes -o ConnectTimeout=10
      -o ServerAliveInterval=15 -o ServerAliveCountMax=3
      -o ControlPath=none -R 127.0.0.1:24817:127.0.0.1:22
      you@server.example
    </p>
    <p class="ui__card-top">
      <span>
        2. To keep it running after a restart. That machine runs
        <span class="ui__select">Linux</span>
      </span>
    </p>
    <p class="ui__card-top">
      <span>
        3. Optional. So that machine's key can hold the link and do
        nothing else on the server, put this in front of its line in
        your account's authorized_keys file on the server, then a
        space.
      </span>
      <span class="ui__button">Copy</span>
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
